  "description": "BUQZAP crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C54 H44 Ho4 O21 2+,2(Cl1 O4 1-),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ho1 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho2 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho3 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho4 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho5 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho6 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho7 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho8 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.465-3.717 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.21-115.68°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ho4(μ4-O)(μ2-OH)2(μ2-L)6](ClO4)2·2H2O (L = 2,6-diformyl-p-cresolate); CCDC C54H44Ho4O21 2+, 2(ClO4−), 2(H2O). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ2-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
